---
import AdSlot from '../../components/AdSlot.astro';
import LoanByVisa from '../../components/LoanByVisa.astro';
import RelatedPosts from '../../components/RelatedPosts.astro';
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Korean Loans by Visa: What Your Status Actually Changes"
  description="Pick your residence status and see what a Korean lender is really deciding — the three screens in order, what your visa genuinely changes, and which products name it in their own published terms."
>
  <header class="mb-8">
    <h1 class="mb-3 font-display text-4xl font-bold text-ink">
      Korean loans by visa
    </h1>
    <p class="max-w-2xl text-slate-600">
      “Which visa qualifies for a loan?” is the question almost everyone
      arrives with, and it is the wrong one — Korean law has no list of
      loan-eligible residence statuses. This shows what your status genuinely
      changes in a lender’s read, and what is deciding the file instead.
    </p>
  </header>

  <LoanByVisa />

  <AdSlot position="bottom" />

  <RelatedPosts category="loans" heading="Guides on loans in Korea" />
</Layout>
